1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,178
We start on the dashboard.

2
00:00:02,178 --> 00:00:04,923
Two things go wrong in every logistics

3
00:00:04,923 --> 00:00:07,812
business: stock that quietly disappears,

4
00:00:07,812 --> 00:00:10,124
and deliveries nobody can prove.

5
00:00:10,124 --> 00:00:11,857
Both are on this screen.

6
00:00:11,857 --> 00:00:13,880
What is below reorder level,

7
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:16,480
and what is waiting to be confirmed.

8
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,050
Inventory here is live, not a monthly

9
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:20,942
spreadsheet.

10
00:00:20,942 --> 00:00:24,435
Every product carries its stock, its warehouse,

11
00:00:24,435 --> 00:00:26,590
and where it physically sits.

12
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:30,901
Scan a label, and it answers the only question

13
00:00:30,901 --> 00:00:33,920
that matters on the floor. Which shelf.

14
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:38,149
You can correct the shelf right here,

15
00:00:38,149 --> 00:00:39,772
and it saves instantly.

16
00:00:39,772 --> 00:00:43,016
So the next person does not walk the aisle for

17
00:00:43,016 --> 00:00:43,580
nothing.

18
00:00:44,330 --> 00:00:47,594
Goods arriving are recorded as a movement,

19
00:00:47,594 --> 00:00:48,916
not an overwrite.

20
00:00:48,916 --> 00:00:52,180
So every unit has a history you can trace.

21
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:56,177
At month end, stocktaking compares what the

22
00:00:56,177 --> 00:00:59,225
system believes against what is actually on

23
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:02,484
the shelf, and posts the gap as an adjustment.

24
00:01:02,484 --> 00:01:03,760
Not a silent edit.

25
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:08,397
Now it ships. The office creates the dispatch,

26
00:01:08,397 --> 00:01:10,331
and assigns the driver.

27
00:01:10,331 --> 00:01:12,601
Only the office can assign.

28
00:01:12,601 --> 00:01:15,880
A driver cannot assign themselves work.

29
00:01:18,930 --> 00:01:20,596
The driver picks it up.

30
00:01:20,596 --> 00:01:23,783
When they arrive, they photograph the signed

31
00:01:23,783 --> 00:01:25,304
waybill on the phone.

32
00:01:25,304 --> 00:01:28,709
The consignee's signature, the date, the goods,

33
00:01:28,709 --> 00:01:30,230
captured at the door.

34
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:35,125
And this is the part that changes everything.

35
00:01:35,125 --> 00:01:37,610
It does not count as delivered yet.

36
00:01:37,610 --> 00:01:39,810
The office gets a notification,

37
00:01:39,810 --> 00:01:42,934
opens the proof, and checks the photo before

38
00:01:42,934 --> 00:01:44,070
closing the run.

39
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:47,377
Only then is it delivered.

40
00:01:47,377 --> 00:01:50,766
The driver's word is not the record.

41
00:01:50,766 --> 00:01:51,990
The photo is.

42
00:01:53,130 --> 00:01:55,638
Roles decide who can do what.

43
00:01:55,638 --> 00:01:58,146
A driver sees their own runs.

44
00:01:58,146 --> 00:02:00,481
Only an owner assigns work,

45
00:02:00,481 --> 00:02:02,470
or confirms a delivery.

46
00:02:03,230 --> 00:02:06,313
And every action is logged against a name.

47
00:02:06,313 --> 00:02:09,323
That is what accounted for actually looks

48
00:02:09,323 --> 00:02:09,690
like.
